  "summary": "Samori Toure was a Mande war leader who built the Wassoulou (Wassulu) Empire in the upper Niger region, with its capital at Bissandugu, and resisted French advance for years. The French captured him in September 1898 and exiled him; he died in exile on 2 June 1900.",
